      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). The 1600 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions or severe pain\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for analgesia\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical rationale, and I'll add it to the order note. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
